Note: Flow core library — the essential, general-purpose builtins: printing,
Note: formatting, arithmetic, comparison, logic, conversions, strings, dictionaries
Note: and (via @collections) lists. Import it with `use "@core"`; the language has
Note: almost nothing without it. @std imports it and adds the rest.
Note: The C# implementations are linked at runtime.

use "@collections"

internal proc print (String: s)
Note: Phase 44 Plan 44-08 — Void-wildcard print overload for the pre-strict
Note: bug fix per ROADMAP line 404. (print 42) charitably auto-strs in
Note: non-strict; emits [strict] (print) requires String — got <Type>
Note: in strict files. The String overload above scores +1000 vs this
Note: wildcard's +500 so (print "hello") stays byte-identical.
internal proc print (Void: s)

Note: Nothing() returns Void. Use as `return (Nothing)` to explicitly
Note: return Void from a proc that would otherwise collect non-void
Note: expressions before its end. There is no Void literal in source;
Note: this is the canonical escape hatch.
internal proc Nothing ()

internal proc len (Voids: arr)
internal proc len(String: s)
internal proc length (Voids: arr)
internal proc length (String: s)

Note: str overloads for all types
internal proc str (Int: value)
internal proc str (Long: value)
internal proc str (Float: value)
internal proc str (Double: value)
internal proc str (Number: value)
internal proc str (String: value)
internal proc str (Bool: value)
internal proc str (Symbol: value)
internal proc str (Voids: value)
internal proc str (Tuple: value)
internal proc str (Dict<Void, Void>: value)

internal proc concat (String: a, String: b)

Note: Type conversions
internal proc intToDouble (Int: value)
internal proc doubleToInt (Double: value)

Note: Phase 44 Plan 44-09 Task 2 — primitive numeric cross-casts. Without these
Note: strict-mode composers have no escape hatch for cross-type comparisons:
Note: `(double 1)` would fail overload resolution because Int → Double widening
Note: is disabled under strict (Plan 44-03). Each of the 4 extractors accepts
Note: every primitive numeric source. Narrowing floors per StdLib.DoubleToInt
Note: convention.
Note:
Note: Identity casts ((double Double), (int Int), ...) are included: without them
Note: (double 2.5) was ambiguous between the unit-typed overloads.
internal proc double (Int: value)
internal proc double (Long: value)
internal proc double (Float: value)
internal proc double (Double: value)

internal proc float (Int: value)
internal proc float (Long: value)
internal proc float (Double: value)
internal proc float (Float: value)

internal proc int (Long: value)
internal proc int (Float: value)
internal proc int (Double: value)
internal proc int (Int: value)

internal proc long (Int: value)
internal proc long (Float: value)
internal proc long (Double: value)
internal proc long (Long: value)

Note: Arithmetic — 5-type same-type fast paths
internal proc add (Int: a, Int: b)
internal proc add (Long: a, Long: b)
internal proc add (Float: a, Float: b)
internal proc add (Double: a, Double: b)
internal proc add (Number: a, Number: b)

internal proc sub (Int: a, Int: b)
internal proc sub (Long: a, Long: b)
internal proc sub (Float: a, Float: b)
internal proc sub (Double: a, Double: b)
internal proc sub (Number: a, Number: b)

internal proc mul (Int: a, Int: b)
internal proc mul (Long: a, Long: b)
internal proc mul (Float: a, Float: b)
internal proc mul (Double: a, Double: b)
internal proc mul (Number: a, Number: b)

Note: (div Int Int) auto-promotes to Double; use (idiv) for Int truncation
internal proc div (Int: a, Int: b)
internal proc div (Long: a, Long: b)
internal proc div (Float: a, Float: b)
internal proc div (Double: a, Double: b)
internal proc div (Number: a, Number: b)

Note: Negation — 5-pack
internal proc neg (Int: x)
internal proc neg (Long: x)
internal proc neg (Float: x)
internal proc neg (Double: x)
internal proc neg (Number: x)

Note: Integer division (truncating)
internal proc idiv (Int: a, Int: b)
internal proc mod (Int: a, Int: b)
internal proc mod (Double: a, Double: b)
internal proc split (String: s, String: separator)

Note: String-to-number conversions
internal proc stringToInt (String: s)
internal proc stringToDouble (String: s)

Note: Lazy evaluation
internal proc eval (Lazy<Void>: value)

internal proc if (Bool: cond, Lazy<Void>: if_true, Lazy<Void>: otherwise)
internal proc if (Bool: cond, Void: if_true, Void: otherwise)
Note: Phase 44 Plan 44-08 — Void-wildcard if for non-strict truthy-coerce
Note: (if 5 ...) / (if "" ...). Strict (CallerStrictMode==true) emits
Note: [strict] (if) requires Bool — got <Type>. Existing Bool-Lazy and
Note: Bool-Void overloads score +1000 for the Bool case.
internal proc if (Void: cond, Void: if_true, Void: otherwise)
internal proc and (Lazy<Bool>: left, Lazy<Bool>: right)
internal proc and (Bool: left, Bool: right)
Note: Phase 44 Plan 44-08 — D-12 last-truthy and (composer Area 4.2 choice).
Note: (and 1 "foo") → "foo"; (and false 1) → false. Bool-Bool overload above
Note: wins +1000 for the Bool case so existing call sites are byte-identical.
internal proc and (Void: left, Void: right)

internal proc or (Lazy<Bool>: left, Lazy<Bool>: right)
internal proc or (Bool: left, Bool: right)
Note: Phase 44 Plan 44-08 — D-12 last-truthy or. (or false 42) → 42;
Note: (or "" "fallback") → "fallback".
internal proc or (Void: left, Void: right)

Note: Phase 44 Plan 44-08 — (not) FIRST registration per RESEARCH A6.
Note: Non-strict charitable truthy: (not 0) → true, (not "x") → false.
Note: Strict emits [strict] (not) requires Bool — got <Type>.
internal proc not (Void: x)

Note: Equality and comparison operators
internal proc equals (Void: a, Void: b)
internal proc sequals (Void: a, Void: b)
internal proc lt (Void: a, Void: b)
internal proc gt (Void: a, Void: b)
internal proc lte (Void: a, Void: b)
internal proc gte (Void: a, Void: b)

Note: Tuple unpack runtime apply
internal proc unpack (Void: tup, Function: f)

Note: Dict ops
Note: Use Dict<Void, Void> in proc decls so the parameter type is structurally a DictType
Note: (matches the runtime impl shape) — distinguishes from the existing Array overloads
Note: of (each)/(map)/(filter)/(size)/(keys)/(values).
internal proc dict (Void...: pairs)
internal proc dictTuple (Void...: tuplePairs)
internal proc get (Dict<Void, Void>: d, Void: k)
internal proc getOr (Dict<Void, Void>: d, Void: k, Void: defaultValue)
internal proc set (Dict<Void, Void>: d, Void: k, Void: v)
internal proc remove (Dict<Void, Void>: d, Void: k)
internal proc has (Dict<Void, Void>: d, Void: k)
internal proc keys (Dict<Void, Void>: d)
internal proc values (Dict<Void, Void>: d)
internal proc size (Dict<Void, Void>: d)
internal proc merge (Dict<Void, Void>: d1, Dict<Void, Void>: d2)
internal proc each (Dict<Void, Void>: d, Function: cb)
internal proc map (Dict<Void, Void>: d, Function: cb)
internal proc filter (Dict<Void, Void>: d, Function: pred)

Note: Iteration guard
internal proc setMaxIterations (Int: limit)

Note: break-control (0615) — (break) / (continue) call-position loop control.
Note: Valid inside while/for bodies including lazy-wrapped positions (if/and/or).
Note: (break) outside any loop is a charitable no-op + one-shot advisory.
internal proc break ()
internal proc continue ()

